1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,264
This is Parallax Print.

2
00:00:02,508 --> 00:00:06,513
A flat image becomes printable pieces for two walls and a floor.

3
00:00:06,792 --> 00:00:09,706
From the chosen viewpoint, everything lines up.

4
00:00:11,111 --> 00:00:14,362
Move around the installation and the image breaks apart.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:16,579
The figure marks the viewing position.

6
00:00:16,788 --> 00:00:20,863
Select Meet the eye level, and the picture comes together again.

7
00:00:22,264 --> 00:00:24,075
Start with an editable example.

8
00:00:24,319 --> 00:00:28,336
Explore a tight fold, a wide corner, or walls with different heights.

9
00:00:28,661 --> 00:00:30,855
You can change the artwork independently.

10
00:00:42,161 --> 00:00:43,949
Open the sample in the editor.

11
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:47,850
Enter the measurements of your own corner, then place the viewing point.

12
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:50,985
These measurements determine how the image is projected.

13
00:00:54,316 --> 00:00:58,043
Upload a PNG or JPEG, or try the included artwork.

14
00:00:58,368 --> 00:01:02,350
Drag the image to compose it, and fine tune its size and rotation.

15
00:01:10,205 --> 00:01:13,978
Switch to Pieces to see the printable shapes for each surface.

16
00:01:14,257 --> 00:01:19,354
These stretched shapes become a single image when they are installed and viewed from the right spot.

17
00:01:20,756 --> 00:01:24,448
Review the warnings, choose your paper, and generate the kit.

18
00:01:24,773 --> 00:01:29,638
Download tiled PDFs, calibration sheets, and an installation guide.

19
00:01:29,963 --> 00:01:33,434
Always check your printed scale before mounting the pieces.

20
00:01:48,503 --> 00:01:51,173
Your artwork and projects stay in your browser.

21
00:01:51,498 --> 00:01:54,958
Parallax Print is a digital alpha, ready to explore.

22
00:01:55,283 --> 00:01:57,977
Try a corner at parallax print dot app.
